*Types of VM:
1. VM:
--> A Virtual Machine (VM) is a virtual computer created inside a physical computer.
It has its own operating system, CPU, memory, and storage

2. VMSS:
--> VMSS is an Azure service used to create and manage a group of identical Virtual Machines.
The number of VMs can automatically increase or decrease according to the workload.

3. Hybrid, preconfigured and high volume solution
--> is a ready-to-use solution in which the operating system, 
software, and required settings are already configured.

**Availability Options:
--> Availability options in Azure define how Azure protects your Virtual Machine from
hardware failure and data-center problems.

1. No Infrastructure Redundancy
--> In this option, your VM runs on one physical server inside an Azure data center.
If the physical host has a hardware problem, your VM may be affected.
2. Availability Zone
--> An Availability Zone is a separate physical location within an Azure region.
If one zone has a problem, your application can continue running in another zone.

